  i Use ?? instead of ||.
  
    31 │ declare const obj: Date | null;
    32 │ declare const fallbackObj: Date;
  > 33 │ const r9 = obj || fallbackObj;
       │                ^^
    34 │ 
    35 │ // `any` and `unknown`: not reported
  
  i The || operator checks for all falsy values (including 0, '', and false), while ?? only checks for null and undefined.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Safe fix: Replace || with ??.
  
